-- title:
--   Theorem 3.4 for $F_2$: $F_2 \cong F$ with $X_n \mapsto X_n$
-- statement:
--   There is a group isomorphism from the presented group $F_2$ onto Thompson's group $F$
--   (the subgroup of order isomorphisms of $[0,1]$ generated by the Thompson maps of the §1
--   bundle) sending each formal symbol $X_n$ to the function $X_n$ of the §2 bundle
--   ($X_0 = A$, $X_n = A^{-(n-1)} B A^{n-1}$). Existence of such an isomorphism is asserted, nothing
--   about uniqueness.
-- source:
--   Cannon, J. W., Floyd, W. J., Parry, W. R., Introductory notes on Richard Thompson's groups, L'Enseignement Mathématique (2) 42 (1996) 215–256, https://doi.org/10.5169/seals-87877, section 3, p. 226, Theorem 3.4 (the F₂ half)

